# Cursor Rule: Font Intelligence

When working on typography, fonts, UI design, CSS styling, or design systems, use the **Font Intelligence Typography Decision System**.

## Canonical Source of Truth
Follow the detailed protocol in:
👉 [`.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md`](file:///d:/font-intelligence/.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md)

## Activation Triggers
Apply this rule when:
- Creating or editing font tokens, `@font-face` rules, or CSS typography properties (`font-family`, `font-weight`, `letter-spacing`, `line-height`).
- Designing new pages, components, SaaS dashboards, or mobile views.
- Choosing font pairings or establishing heading/body hierarchy.
- Verifying font licensing or multi-language script coverage.

## Quick CLI Reference
```bash
# Get recommendations for a project
python scripts/recommend.py --use-case <id> --style "<vibe>" --platform <web|flutter|powerpoint>

# Score a candidate pairing
python scripts/score_pair.py --primary <id> --secondary <id> --style <vibe>

# Search catalog fonts
python scripts/search_fonts.py --mood "<vibe>" --role <body> --min-readability 8
```

## Offline / Fast Fallback
If Python is unavailable or context is limited:
- Inspect `catalog/fonts.json` and `catalog/pairings.json`.
- Refer to [`lite/font-intelligence-lite.md`](file:///d:/font-intelligence/lite/font-intelligence-lite.md).

## Non-Negotiable Hard Rules
1. Never invent fonts, weights, or language scripts.
2. Never assign decorative fonts to body/UI text.
3. Respect explicit user font preferences.
4. Limit to 2 primary font families (plus monospace only for code/telemetry).
5. Always provide robust generic system fallbacks.
